# Core App — frontend environment variables (Vite).
# Copy to `.env` for local development, or set the same names in the
# Vercel project settings (Settings → Environment Variables) for
# Production/Preview. Values below are placeholders only.
#
# --- Supabase project roles (see docs/supabase-projects.md) ---
# MAIN / ACTIVE : pundggjzzaqzbvykbxvo  ← local `.env` / current development only
# TEST (inactive): hnfvrlgcnpykncixxqha ← preserve; do not use until testing phase
# Do not point VITE_SUPABASE_* at TEST during development. Do not mix MAIN
# and TEST keys. CLI cache under supabase/.temp/ may name TEST — ignore it
# for app runtime; do not relink or run db CLI against it in this phase.
#
# Vercel note: if your project instead contains SUPABASE_URL and
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY (e.g. provisioned by the Vercel Supabase
# integration, without the VITE_ prefix), the Vite build maps those
# two public values automatically — either naming works, VITE_*
# takes precedence. A redeploy is required after any change.
#
# Both variables are safe to expose in the browser: the anon key is
# protected by Supabase Row Level Security. NEVER put a Supabase
# service-role key or any private provider secret in a VITE_* variable.

# MAIN PRODUCTION project URL (placeholder — replace YOUR_PROJECT_REF
# with the Production ref when creating a real `.env`, currently
# pundggjzzaqzbvykbxvo for this product).
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=YOUR_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY

# --- Optional FUTURE TEST credentials (NOT used by Vite app runtime) ---
# If you create a gitignored `.env.test.local` for `npm run test:supabase`,
# use the FUTURE TEST project only (hnfvrlgcnpykncixxqha). Hosted test
# scripts refuse to run when SUPABASE_TEST_URL is the Production ref.
# SUPABASE_TEST_URL=https://YOUR_FUTURE_TEST_REF.supabase.co
# VITE_SUPABASE_TEST_URL=https://YOUR_FUTURE_TEST_REF.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_TEST_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=YOUR_TEST_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY
# VITE_SUPABASE_TEST_ANON_KEY=YOUR_TEST_ANON_KEY
